🚨 **BLOCKING: re-inlines the tracker holder that gh-1244 just canonicalized in `common/trackers.js`**

This PR replaces the previous one-line delegate (`return trackersModule.createTrackerHolder();`) with a full inlined copy of the lazy holder. But main has since moved: gh-1244 (PR #1253, commit `5e46da6a`) placed the canonical `createTrackerHolder()` in `js/common/trackers.js` (see its docstring there) and converted ~24 production callers to:

```javascript
var trackerHolder = trackersModule.createTrackerHolder();
var initTracker = trackerHolder.initTracker;
var getTracker = trackerHolder.getTracker;
```

Keeping this inlined copy means two canonical implementations of the same holder again (the thing gh-1246 is deleting), and `js/postTestReworkResults.js:33` — which this PR switched from `trackersModule.createTrackerHolder()` to `shared.createTrackerHolder(trackersModule)` — is one of the two files that currently conflict with main (verified via `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main HEAD` → content conflict in `js/postTestReworkResults.js`).

**Fix**: after merging main, restore the delegate shape here —

```javascript
function createTrackerHolder(trackersModule) {
    // gh-1244: canonical implementation lives in common/trackers.js.
    return trackersModule.createTrackerHolder();
}
```

— and switch `postTestReworkResults.js`, `postStoryTestAutomationResults.js` and `postStoryTestAutomationReview.js` to destructure `trackersModule.createTrackerHolder()` directly, matching the pattern every other post-action now uses.

